---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import logo from "../assets/brand/logo.png";
import { REPO_URL } from "../lib/release";
---

<Base
  title="privacy policy · ramus"
  description="What the ramus music player does and doesn't do with your data: no tracking, no analytics, no data collection."
>
  <header class="wrap policy-top">
    <a class="policy-top__brand" href="/" aria-label="ramus, home">
      <Image src={logo} alt="" width={64} height={64} class="policy-top__mark" loading="eager" />
      <span>ramus</span>
    </a>
  </header>

  <main id="main" class="section policy-page">
    <article class="wrap policy">
      <h1 class="headline">
        privacy policy. <span class="more">ramus collects nothing about you.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="policy__date mono">effective 10 october 2026</p>

      <p class="lede">
        ramus is a free, open-source music player for plex. it has no accounts of its own, no analytics, no advertising, no
        tracking and no crash reporting, and its developer runs no servers. nothing you do in ramus is sent to its developer.
      </p>

      <h2>what ramus talks to</h2>
      <p>only what it needs to play your music:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>plex.tv</strong>, when you sign in with your plex account and when ramus looks up your servers and players.
          requests carry the standard plex client details: the app's name, the platform and device type, and a random
          identifier ramus creates the first time it runs. plex's side is covered by
          the <a href="https://www.plex.tv/about/privacy-legal/">plex privacy policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>your plex media server</strong>, to browse, stream and download your own music and to report playback
          progress. your server uses those reports to count plays, and may pass them on to services you've linked to your
          plex account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>lrclib</strong> (lrclib.net), to look up lyrics when your plex server has none for a track. ramus sends the
          track's title, artist, album and duration, and nothing that identifies you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>other plex players</strong>, only when you cast to one. ramus sends the player playback commands and a
          temporary access token from your plex account so it can stream from your server; your long-lived sign-in token
          never leaves your device.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>links to the source code and licences open in your browser only when you tap them.</p>

      <h2>what stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>your plex sign-in token, stored encrypted (in the keychain on iPhone).</li>
        <li>
          a copy of your library's details and artwork, your settings, your play queue, and any music you download or ramus
          caches for smooth playback, all in the app's own storage.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>signing out deletes the sign-in token and the play queue. uninstalling ramus deletes everything else it stored.</p>

      <h2>this website</h2>
      <p>
        ramusplayer.app has no cookies, analytics or trackers. it's hosted on github pages, which keeps standard server
        logs under <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">github's
        privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>children</h2>
      <p>ramus isn't aimed at children, and it collects no information from anyone.</p>

      <h2>changes</h2>
      <p>if this policy changes, the new version goes up on this page with a new effective date.</p>

      <h2>contact</h2>
      <p>
        questions go to <a href="mailto:admin@blueshelter.net">admin@blueshelter.net</a> or
        the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>issue tracker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* The muted tint of the home page's privacy section; this page has no
     sections for the scroll-driven tint to follow. */
  :root {
    --tint-a: #1c1b22;
    --tint-b: #23202b;
  }
</style>

<style>
  .policy-top {
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .policy-top__brand {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    font: 700 1.3rem/1 var(--font-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .policy-top__mark {
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
  }

  .policy-page {
    padding-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .policy {
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
    margin-inline: auto;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .policy :where(h1) {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .policy__date {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .policy h2 + p,
  .policy h2 + ul {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  .policy ul {
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .policy li + li {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  .policy ul + p {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
  }

  .policy strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
